# GitHub Workflow

Git commits/branches: `git-workflow-and-versioning`. Issues/PRs/labels/assignees: this rule.

When creating or editing GitHub issues or PRs, load `.cursor/skills/github-workflow/SKILL.md`. Do not improvise `gh` flags.

## Linked bodies — tick before merge

Scope is the **PR body** and every issue the PR names (`Closes` / `Fixes` / `Resolves` #N). Open vs closed does not matter. Tick **before** `gh pr merge`. After merge is too late.

```bash
gh issue view N --json title,body,comments
gh pr view N --json title,body,comments
```

`- [ ]` is unfinished work. Do it, PATCH to `- [x]`, then this must print nothing (else do not merge):

```bash
if gh api "repos/OWNER/REPO/issues/N" --jq .body | grep -E '^[[:space:]]*- \[ \]'; then
  exit 1
fi
```

Run that on the PR number and every linked issue number.

## Standard GitHub flow (mandatory on these use cases)

When a use case below matches, follow the full flow. Do not skip it to "avoid spam":

`issue (reuse or create) → branch → PR with Closes #N → label + assignee → tick body checklists → review → green checks → merge`

**Use it for:**
- the user asked for GitHub flow / an issue / a PR
- a bug that needs a durable repro and acceptance
- a feature that needs acceptance criteria
- work that spans (or will span) more than one PR
- other collaborators will review, or the change is breaking / security-sensitive / public behavior
- CI, install, or shared automation
- an **open** issue already covers this work (join it; `Closes #N`)

**Do not** open an issue for a one-file chore, typo, comment, or "so the PR has a number." If none of the use cases match, a labeled PR is enough. Never invent `Closes`.

## Discover, don't invent

Before any GitHub write:

```bash
gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,defaultBranchRef
gh label list
gh api "repos/$(gh repo view --json nameWithOwner -q .nameWithOwner)/collaborators" --jq '.[].login'
```

Never create labels. Never assign or request-review a login that is not in that list. Never request review from the PR author.

## Labels

Exactly one type label if it exists in `gh label list`: `bug` | `enhancement` | `chore` | `documentation`. Add `automated` only on bot/sync PRs. If the type is missing, ask.

## Assign and review

- Assignee: `--assignee "@me"` when the authenticated user is a collaborator. If other humans have push, ask who owns it.
- **Ask before** a GitHub review when the diff is large or touches more than a few files.
- Small diffs: review if the user asked to ship. Solo: `gh pr review --comment` — never `--approve` your own PR.
- Merge only after `gh pr checks` is green and required checkboxes are ticked.
